        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in /api/tools/ping Endpoint: **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the application via the JSON request body key `host` extracted using `data = request.get_json() or {}` and `host = data.get('host', '')` at lines 106-107.\n\n**Sanitization/Validation**: The endpoint only checks whether `host` is truthy/non-empty (`if not host:`). It performs no validation against an IP address or hostname format and does not sanitize or escape shell metacharacters.\n\n**Sink**: `exit_code = os.system(command)` on line 114 executes `command = f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"` directly in a system shell.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nAn attacker can provide shell command chaining operators (such as `;`, `&`, or `|`) inside the `host` JSON field:\n```http\nPOST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n    \"host\": \"127.0.0.1; id\"\n}\n```\nWhen executed by `os.system(\"ping -c 1 127.0.0.1; id\")`, the shell will execute `ping -c 1 127.0.0.1` followed immediately by the arbitrary command `id`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 114
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-78",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in /api/tools/ping Endpoint: **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the application via the JSON request body key `host` extracted using `data = request.get_json() or {}` and `host = data.get('host', '')` at lines 106-107.\n\n**Sanitization/Validation**: The endpoint only checks whether `host` is truthy/non-empty (`if not host:`). It performs no validation against an IP address or hostname format and does not sanitize or escape shell metacharacters.\n\n**Sink**: `exit_code = os.system(command)` on line 114 executes `command = f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"` directly in a system shell.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nAn attacker can provide shell command chaining operators (such as `;`, `&`, or `|`) inside the `host` JSON field:\n```http\nPOST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n    \"host\": \"127.0.0.1; id\"\n}\n```\nWhen executed by `os.system(\"ping -c 1 127.0.0.1; id\")`, the shell will execute `ping -c 1 127.0.0.1` followed immediately by the arbitrary command `id`."
          },
          "locations": [
