              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in /api/user/search Endpoint: **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the application via the query parameter `username` obtained with `username = request.args.get('username', '')` on line 65.\n\n**Sanitization/Validation**: No sanitization, escaping, or parameterization is performed on `username`. The value is directly embedded into the SQL query string using Python f-string interpolation: `f\"SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '{username}'\"`.\n\n**Sink**: The interpolated query string is passed to `cursor.execute(query)` on line 72 and executed against the SQLite database.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nAn attacker can send an HTTP GET request containing SQL injection metacharacters to alter query logic or extract data via UNION queries:\n```http\nGET /api/user/search?username='%20OR%20'1'='1 HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\n```\nThis causes the executed SQL query to become:\n`SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '' OR '1'='1'`\nwhich bypasses the username filter and returns all user records from the database."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 70,
                  "endLine": 72
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) in /api/documents/<doc_id>: **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the application via the path parameter `doc_id` in `/api/documents/<int:doc_id>` and the `X-User-ID` request header.\n\n**Sanitization/Validation**: The endpoint verifies that the `X-User-ID` header is present (`if not current_user_id: return jsonify(...), 401`), but performs no authorization checks to verify that the requesting user (`current_user_id`) is the owner of the document or possesses the required permissions to view it.\n\n**Sink**: `cursor.execute(\"SELECT id, owner_id, title, content FROM documents WHERE id = ?\", (doc_id,))` on line 92 retrieves the document solely based on `doc_id`, and line 98 returns the full document content to the caller regardless of document ownership.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nAn unprivileged user with user ID 3 (Bob) can access confidential documents owned by user ID 1 (Admin) by querying their document ID:\n```http\nGET /api/documents/1 HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\nX-User-ID: 3\n```\nThe server will return HTTP 200 with the full content of Document 1 (\"Super Secret Admin Report\"), bypassing access control restrictions."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 92,
                  "endLine": 93
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in /api/user/search Endpoint: **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the application via the query parameter `username` obtained with `username = request.args.get('username', '')` on line 65.\n\n**Sanitization/Validation**: No sanitization, escaping, or parameterization is performed on `username`. The value is directly embedded into the SQL query string using Python f-string interpolation: `f\"SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '{username}'\"`.\n\n**Sink**: The interpolated query string is passed to `cursor.execute(query)` on line 72 and executed against the SQLite database.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nAn attacker can send an HTTP GET request containing SQL injection metacharacters to alter query logic or extract data via UNION queries:\n```http\nGET /api/user/search?username='%20OR%20'1'='1 HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\n```\nThis causes the executed SQL query to become:\n`SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '' OR '1'='1'`\nwhich bypasses the username filter and returns all user records from the database."
          },
